## E1 (L4) — The graveyard, built (with the selection equation)

Build a 400-stock synthetic world, 15 years monthly: each stock has
a persistent drift μᵢ ~ N(10%, 5%) (this makes momentum REAL);
monthly hazard of death ~0.5%/mo at the mean but HIGHER for
low-drift stocks (deaths correlate with performance — that's the
selection equation); a dying stock's final month returns −30%
(Shumway's delisting return), then it is gone. Store death months.
Print: survivors vs dead at year 15, and corr(μᵢ, months alive).

